
# The app host: boot the routed app, env-abstracted. The SAME `route(host, path)` dispatcher drives both sides; only
# this `host` differs per environment (the native-env mechanism picks browser vs node). The browser mounts the matched
# page on the document body and re-renders on navigation; the server starts an HTTP server that renders each request
# through `route` and responds with HTML (SSR). This is the one client/server seam -- the app author writes neither.

load ../../dom/view
  find view

task host
  take route
    like task
      take host, like view
      take path, like text
  take port, like number
